  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#deadweight">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Deadweight</rdfs:label>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Deadweight</skos:prefLabel>
    <nltl:draftConceptId>VOC-0185</nltl:draftConceptId>
    <nltl:stage1LocalName>deadweightTonnes</nltl:stage1LocalName>
    <nltl:module rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#moduleHull"/>
    <nltl:roleDecisionBasis>Quantity metadata requires the canonical QUDT QuantityValue node pattern</nltl:roleDecisionBasis>
    <nltl:namingBasis>Locked-workbook normalized regulatory term</nltl:namingBasis>
    <nltl:namingRule>N4 - preserve the source concept; normalize spelling to ASCII lowerCamelCase</nltl:namingRule>
    <nltl:unitDecisionStatus>Verified recommended QUDT unit from Stage 1 or a documented Stage 2 source-unit refinement</nltl:unitDecisionStatus>
    <nltl:stage2UnitEvidence>IMO-110 explicitly states the applicability threshold as 5,000 tonnes deadweight</nltl:stage2UnitEvidence>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for deadweightTonnes derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <nltl:sourceReference>IMO-110 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.41 | 1.2.3</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>For category A and B oil tankers of less than 5,000 tonnes deadweight constructed on or after 1 January 2017, the entire cargo tank length shall be protected with: double bottom tanks or spaces complying with the applicable requirements of regulation 19.6.1 of MARPOL Annex I; and wing tanks or spaces arranged in accordance with regulation 19.3.1 of MARPOL An...</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
    <skos:altLabel>deadweight_tonnes</skos:altLabel>
    <nltl:sourceAlias>deadweight_tonnes</nltl:sourceAlias>
    <nltl:sourceRequirementId>IMO-110</nltl:sourceRequirementId>
    <nltl:unitSymbol>t</nltl:unitSymbol>
    <nltl:recommendedUnit rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TON_Metric"/>
    <nltl:quantityKindLabel>Mass</nltl:quantityKindLabel>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#supportingStructure">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hullStructure"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Supporting structure</rdfs:label>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Supporting structure</skos:prefLabel>
    <nltl:draftConceptId>VOC-0737</nltl:draftConceptId>
    <nltl:stage1LocalName>supportingStructure</nltl:stage1LocalName>
    <nltl:module rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#moduleHull"/>
    <nltl:roleDecisionBasis>Explicit engineering entity/artifact class set</nltl:roleDecisionBasis>
    <nltl:namingBasis>Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term</nltl:namingBasis>
    <nltl:namingRule>N5 - component or subject first, followed by characteristic and qualifier/state; no unsupported external mapping</nltl:namingRule>
    <nltl:unitDecisionStatus>Not a quantity property</nltl:unitDecisionStatus>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for supportingStructure derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <nltl:sourceReference>TRF-046 | TRAFICOM p.19 | 4.4.2.2; TRF-047 | TRAFICOM p.20 | 4.4.2.3; TRF-049 | TRAFICOM p.21 | 4.4.4.1</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>The upper end of the strengthened part of a main frame and of an intermediate ice frame shall be attached to a deck, top or bottom plating of a tank or an ice stringer (section 4.5). Where a frame terminates above a deck or a stringer which is situated at or above the upper limit of the ice belt (section 4.3.1), the part above the deck or stringer may have t...</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
    <skos:altLabel>supportingStructure</skos:altLabel>
    <nltl:sourceAlias>supportingStructure</nltl:sourceAlias>
    <nltl:sourceRequirementId>TRF-046</nltl:sourceRequirementId>
    <nltl:sourceRequirementId>TRF-047</nltl:sourceRequirementId>
    <nltl:sourceRequirementId>TRF-049</nltl:sourceRequirementId>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#equivalentImpactSphereRadius">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Equivalent impact sphere radius</rdfs:label>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Equivalent impact sphere radius</skos:prefLabel>
    <nltl:draftConceptId>VOC-0239</nltl:draftConceptId>
    <nltl:stage1LocalName>equivalentImpactSphereRadius</nltl:stage1LocalName>
    <nltl:module rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#moduleCore"/>
    <nltl:roleDecisionBasis>Formula/comparison or engineering-numeric semantics require a unit-bearing QUDT QuantityValue node</nltl:roleDecisionBasis>
    <nltl:namingBasis>Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term</nltl:namingBasis>
    <nltl:namingRule>N5 - component or subject first, followed by characteristic and qualifier/state; no unsupported external mapping</nltl:namingRule>
    <nltl:unitDecisionStatus>Recommended canonical QUDT unit selected by Stage 2 engineering normalization: Canonical benchmark length unit</nltl:unitDecisionStatus>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for equivalentImpactSphereRadius derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <nltl:sourceReference>TRF-114 | TRAFICOM p.53 | 6.6.5.2; TRF-116 | TRAFICOM p.56 | 6.6.5.2</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>The thruster must withstand the loads occurring when the design ice block defined in Table 6-3 impacts on the thruster body when the ship is sailing at a typical ice operating speed. Load cases for impact loads are given in Table 6-16. The contact geometry is estimated to be hemispherical in shape. If the actual contact geometry differs from the shape of the...</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
    <skos:altLabel>equivalentImpactSphereRadius</skos:altLabel>
    <nltl:sourceAlias>equivalentImpactSphereRadius</nltl:sourceAlias>
    <nltl:sourceRequirementId>TRF-114</nltl:sourceRequirementId>
    <nltl:sourceRequirementId>TRF-116</nltl:sourceRequirementId>
    <nltl:unitSymbol>m</nltl:unitSymbol>
    <nltl:recommendedUnit rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M"/>
    <nltl:quantityKindLabel>Length</nltl:quantityKindLabel>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceLoadHeight">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Ice load height</rdfs:label>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Ice load height</skos:prefLabel>
    <nltl:draftConceptId>VOC-0364</nltl:draftConceptId>
    <nltl:stage1LocalName>iceLoadHeight</nltl:stage1LocalName>
    <nltl:module rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#moduleCore"/>
    <nltl:roleDecisionBasis>Formula/comparison or engineering-numeric semantics require a unit-bearing QUDT QuantityValue node</nltl:roleDecisionBasis>
    <nltl:namingBasis>Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term</nltl:namingBasis>
    <nltl:namingRule>N5 - component or subject first, followed by characteristic and qualifier/state; no unsupported external mapping</nltl:namingRule>
    <nltl:unitDecisionStatus>Recommended canonical QUDT unit selected by Stage 2 engineering normalization: Canonical benchmark length unit</nltl:unitDecisionStatus>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for iceLoadHeight derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <nltl:sourceReference>TRF-057 | TRAFICOM p.23 | 4.6.1</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>The ice load transferred to a web frame from an ice stringer or from longitudinal framing shall be F = f_12*p*h*S [MN] (4.15). When calculating c_a, use l_a = 2*S. If p*h is less than 0.15 MN/m, use 0.15 MN/m. Use f_12 = 1.8.</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
    <skos:altLabel>iceLoadHeight</skos:altLabel>
    <nltl:sourceAlias>iceLoadHeight</nltl:sourceAlias>
    <nltl:sourceRequirementId>TRF-057</nltl:sourceRequirementId>
    <nltl:unitSymbol>m</nltl:unitSymbol>
    <nltl:recommendedUnit rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M"/>
    <nltl:quantityKindLabel>Length</nltl:quantityKindLabel>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#yieldPoint">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Yield point</rdfs:label>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Yield point</skos:prefLabel>
    <nltl:draftConceptId>VOC-0820</nltl:draftConceptId>
    <nltl:stage1LocalName>yieldPoint</nltl:stage1LocalName>
    <nltl:module rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#moduleCore"/>
    <nltl:roleDecisionBasis>Clause-linked engineering quantity override; represented by the canonical QUDT QuantityValue node pattern</nltl:roleDecisionBasis>
    <nltl:namingBasis>Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term</nltl:namingBasis>
    <nltl:namingRule>N5 - component or subject first, followed by characteristic and qualifier/state; no unsupported external mapping</nltl:namingRule>
    <nltl:unitDecisionStatus>Recommended canonical QUDT unit selected by Stage 2 engineering normalization: Canonical benchmark stress/pressure unit</nltl:unitDecisionStatus>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for yieldPoint derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <nltl:sourceReference>TRF-031 | TRAFICOM p.12 | 4.1</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>The acceptance criterion for designs is that the combined stresses from bending and shear, when using the von Mises yield criterion, are lower than the yield point sigmay. When the direct calculation is based on beam theory, the allowable shear stress must be no larger than 0.9*tauy, where tauy = sigmay/sqrt3.</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
    <skos:altLabel>yieldPoint</skos:altLabel>
    <nltl:sourceAlias>yieldPoint</nltl:sourceAlias>
    <nltl:sourceRequirementId>TRF-031</nltl:sourceRequirementId>
    <nltl:unitSymbol>MPa</nltl:unitSymbol>
    <nltl:recommendedUnit rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MegaPA"/>
    <nltl:quantityKindLabel>PressureOrStress</nltl:quantityKindLabel>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#pitchValueKnown">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Pitch value known</rdfs:label>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Pitch value known</skos:prefLabel>
    <nltl:draftConceptId>VOC-0539</nltl:draftConceptId>
    <nltl:stage1LocalName>pitchValueKnown</nltl:stage1LocalName>
    <nltl:module rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#moduleMachinery"/>
    <nltl:roleDecisionBasis>Stage 1 explicit boolean</nltl:roleDecisionBasis>
    <nltl:namingBasis>Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term</nltl:namingBasis>
    <nltl:namingRule>N5 - component or subject first, followed by characteristic and qualifier/state; no unsupported external mapping</nltl:namingRule>
    <nltl:unitDecisionStatus>Not a quantity property</nltl:unitDecisionStatus>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for pitchValueKnown derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <nltl:sourceReference>TRF-084 | TRAFICOM p.38 | 6.5.3.1; TRF-086 | TRAFICOM p.39 | 6.5.3.2</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>For CP propellers, the propeller pitch, P0.7 shall correspond to MCR in bollard condition. If not known, P0.7 shall have a value equal to 0.7*P0.7n, where P0.7n is the propeller pitch at MCR in free running condition.</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
    <skos:altLabel>pitchValueKnown</skos:altLabel>
    <nltl:sourceAlias>pitchValueKnown</nltl:sourceAlias>
    <nltl:sourceRequirementId>TRF-084</nltl:sourceRequirementId>
    <nltl:sourceRequirementId>TRF-086</nltl:sourceRequirementId>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#combinedBendingShearStress">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Combined bending shear stress</rdfs:label>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Combined bending shear stress</skos:prefLabel>
    <nltl:draftConceptId>VOC-0149</nltl:draftConceptId>
    <nltl:stage1LocalName>combinedBendingShearStress</nltl:stage1LocalName>
    <nltl:module rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#moduleCore"/>
    <nltl:roleDecisionBasis>Formula/comparison or engineering-numeric semantics require a unit-bearing QUDT QuantityValue node</nltl:roleDecisionBasis>
    <nltl:namingBasis>Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term</nltl:namingBasis>
    <nltl:namingRule>N5 - component or subject first, followed by characteristic and qualifier/state; no unsupported external mapping</nltl:namingRule>
    <nltl:unitDecisionStatus>Recommended canonical QUDT unit selected by Stage 2 engineering normalization: Canonical benchmark stress/pressure unit</nltl:unitDecisionStatus>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for combinedBendingShearStress derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <nltl:sourceReference>TRF-031 | TRAFICOM p.12 | 4.1</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>The acceptance criterion for designs is that the combined stresses from bending and shear, when using the von Mises yield criterion, are lower than the yield point sigmay. When the direct calculation is based on beam theory, the allowable shear stress must be no larger than 0.9*tauy, where tauy = sigmay/sqrt3.</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
    <skos:altLabel>combinedBendingShearStress</skos:altLabel>
    <nltl:sourceAlias>combinedBendingShearStress</nltl:sourceAlias>
    <nltl:sourceRequirementId>TRF-031</nltl:sourceRequirementId>
