    <nltl:sourceReference>TRF-102 | TRAFICOM p.46 | 6.5.4.2</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>The maximum spindle torque due to a blade-failure load acting at 0.8R shall be determined by appropriate stress analysis or Q_sex = max(C_LE0.8, 0.8*C_TE0.8)*C_spex*F_ex [kNm] (6.36), where C_spex = C_sp*C_fex = 0.7*(1 - ((4*EAR)/Z)^3) (6.37). If C_spex is below 0.3, a value of 0.3 shall be used. C_LE0.8 and C_TE0.8 are the leading-edge and trailing-edge por...</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
    <skos:altLabel>Q_sex_kNm</skos:altLabel>
    <nltl:sourceAlias>Q_sex_kNm</nltl:sourceAlias>
    <nltl:sourceRequirementId>TRF-102</nltl:sourceRequirementId>
    <nltl:unitSymbol>kN*m</nltl:unitSymbol>
    <nltl:recommendedUnit rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloN-M"/>
    <nltl:quantityKindLabel>TorqueOrMoment</nltl:quantityKindLabel>
  </rdf:Description>
