    <nltl:unitDecisionStatus>Recommended canonical QUDT unit selected by Stage 2 engineering normalization: Canonical dimensionless unit</nltl:unitDecisionStatus>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for propellerPowerFraction derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <nltl:sourceReference>TRF-119 | TRAFICOM p.60 | 6.6.5.5</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>Evaluating the global vibratory behavior of the thruster body is important, if the first blade order excitations are in the same frequency range with the thruster global modes of vibration, which occur when the propeller rotational speeds are in the high power range of the propulsion line. This evaluation is mandatory and it must be shown that there is eithe...</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
