    <nltl:sourceReference>I2-003 | IACS_UR_I2 p.1 | I2.1.2.1; I2-004 | IACS_UR_I2 p.1 | I2.1.2.2; TRF-011 | TRAFICOM p.6 | 2.1; TRF-014 | TRAFICOM p.7 | 2.2; TRF-015 | TRAFICOM p.7 | 2.2; TRF-016 | TRAFICOM p.7 | 2.2; TRF-020 | TRAFICOM p.8-9 | 3.2.2; TRF-030 | TRAFICOM p.12 | 4.1; TRF-061 | TRAFICOM p.25 | 4.7</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>The upper ice waterline (UIWL) shall be the envelope of the highest points of the waterlines at which the ship is intended to operate in ice. The line may be a broken line.</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
