    <nltl:stage1LocalName>designVerticalIceShearForce</nltl:stage1LocalName>
    <nltl:module rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#moduleHull"/>
    <nltl:roleDecisionBasis>Formula/comparison or engineering-numeric semantics require a unit-bearing QUDT QuantityValue node</nltl:roleDecisionBasis>
    <nltl:namingBasis>Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term</nltl:namingBasis>
    <nltl:namingRule>N5 - component or subject first, followed by characteristic and qualifier/state; no unsupported external mapping</nltl:namingRule>
    <nltl:unitDecisionStatus>Recommended canonical QUDT unit selected by Stage 2 engineering normalization: Canonical benchmark force/load unit</nltl:unitDecisionStatus>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for designVerticalIceShearForce derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <nltl:sourceReference>I2-051 | IACS_UR_I2 p.19 | I2.13.3.1; I2-053 | IACS_UR_I2 p.20 | I2.13.3.2</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>The design vertical ice shear force, FI, along the hull girder is to be taken as: FI = Cf * FIB [MN] where Cf = longitudinal distribution factor to be taken as follows: (a) Positive shear force Cf = 0.0 between the aft end of LUI and 0.6LUI from aft Cf = 1.0 between 0.9 LUI from aft and the forward end of LUI</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
