  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#beamTheoryUsed">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Beam theory used</rdfs:label>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Beam theory used</skos:prefLabel>
    <nltl:draftConceptId>VOC-0078</nltl:draftConceptId>
    <nltl:stage1LocalName>beamTheoryUsed</nltl:stage1LocalName>
    <nltl:module rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#moduleCore"/>
    <nltl:roleDecisionBasis>Stage 1 explicit boolean</nltl:roleDecisionBasis>
    <nltl:namingBasis>Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term</nltl:namingBasis>
    <nltl:namingRule>N5 - component or subject first, followed by characteristic and qualifier/state; no unsupported external mapping</nltl:namingRule>
    <nltl:unitDecisionStatus>Not a quantity property</nltl:unitDecisionStatus>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for beamTheoryUsed derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <nltl:sourceReference>TRF-031 | TRAFICOM p.12 | 4.1</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>The acceptance criterion for designs is that the combined stresses from bending and shear, when using the von Mises yield criterion, are lower than the yield point sigmay. When the direct calculation is based on beam theory, the allowable shear stress must be no larger than 0.9*tauy, where tauy = sigmay/sqrt3.</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
    <skos:altLabel>beamTheoryUsed</skos:altLabel>
    <nltl:sourceAlias>beamTheoryUsed</nltl:sourceAlias>
    <nltl:sourceRequirementId>TRF-031</nltl:sourceRequirementId>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#coefficientG1">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Coefficient g1</rdfs:label>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Coefficient g1</skos:prefLabel>
    <nltl:draftConceptId>VOC-0144</nltl:draftConceptId>
    <nltl:stage1LocalName>coefficientG1</nltl:stage1LocalName>
    <nltl:module rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#moduleCore"/>
    <nltl:roleDecisionBasis>Formula/comparison or engineering-numeric semantics require a unit-bearing QUDT QuantityValue node</nltl:roleDecisionBasis>
    <nltl:namingBasis>Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term</nltl:namingBasis>
    <nltl:namingRule>N5 - component or subject first, followed by characteristic and qualifier/state; no unsupported external mapping</nltl:namingRule>
    <nltl:unitDecisionStatus>Recommended canonical QUDT unit selected by Stage 2 engineering normalization: Canonical dimensionless unit</nltl:unitDecisionStatus>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for coefficientG1 derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <nltl:sourceReference>TRF-027 | TRAFICOM p.11 | 3.2.4</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>Coefficients f_1-f_4 and g_1-g_3 are given in Table 3-3. C_3 = 460 kg/(m^2*s^2), C_4 = 18.7 kg/(m^2*s^2), C_5 = 825 kg/s^2. If the value of the term ((L*T)/B^2)^3 is less than 5, the value 5 shall be used; if the value is more than 20, the value 20 shall be used.</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
    <skos:altLabel>coefficientG1</skos:altLabel>
    <nltl:sourceAlias>coefficientG1</nltl:sourceAlias>
    <nltl:sourceRequirementId>TRF-027</nltl:sourceRequirementId>
    <nltl:unitSymbol>1</nltl:unitSymbol>
    <nltl:recommendedUnit rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS"/>
    <nltl:quantityKindLabel>DimensionlessRatio</nltl:quantityKindLabel>
  </rdf:Description>
