    <nltl:namingBasis>Verified exact implementation term</nltl:namingBasis>
    <nltl:namingRule>N1 - reuse only after exact URI and semantic-context verification</nltl:namingRule>
    <nltl:unitDecisionStatus>Recommended canonical QUDT unit selected by Stage 2 engineering normalization: Canonical benchmark length unit</nltl:unitDecisionStatus>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for shipLength derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <nltl:sourceReference>TRF-027 | TRAFICOM p.11 | 3.2.4</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>Coefficients f_1-f_4 and g_1-g_3 are given in Table 3-3. C_3 = 460 kg/(m^2*s^2), C_4 = 18.7 kg/(m^2*s^2), C_5 = 825 kg/s^2. If the value of the term ((L*T)/B^2)^3 is less than 5, the value 5 shall be used; if the value is more than 20, the value 20 shall be used.</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
    <skos:altLabel>shipLength</skos:altLabel>
