    <nltl:unitDecisionStatus>Recommended canonical QUDT unit selected by Stage 2 engineering normalization: Canonical benchmark force/load unit</nltl:unitDecisionStatus>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for webFrameIceLoad derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <nltl:sourceReference>TRF-057 | TRAFICOM p.23 | 4.6.1</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>The ice load transferred to a web frame from an ice stringer or from longitudinal framing shall be F = f_12*p*h*S [MN] (4.15). When calculating c_a, use l_a = 2*S. If p*h is less than 0.15 MN/m, use 0.15 MN/m. Use f_12 = 1.8.</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
