    <nltl:sourceReference>IMO-037 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.19 | 4.3.2.1; IMO-067 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.24 | 8.3.1.2; IMO-081 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.26 | 9.3.2.1.1; IMO-085 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.27 | 9.3.2.1.4.2; IMO-108 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.41 | 1.2.1; IMO-109 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.41 | 1.2.2; IMO-110 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.41 | 1.2.3; IMO-111 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.41 | 1.2.4; IMO-114 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.42 | 2.1.3; IMO-118 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.43 | 4.2.2; IMO26-007 | IMO_AMEND_2026 p.3 | 9-1.3.2.1.1; IMO26-011 | IMO_AMEND_2026 p.4 | 9-1.3.2.1.4.2</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>Ships of categories A and B, constructed on or after 1 January 2017, shall be able to withstand flooding resulting from hull penetration due to ice impact. The residual stability following ice damage shall be such that the factor s_i, as defined in SOLAS regulations II-1/7-2.2 and II-1/7-2.3, is equal to one for all loading conditions used to calculate the a...</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
