    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for responseTorque derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <nltl:sourceReference>TRF-097 | TRAFICOM p.43-44 | 6.5.3.4</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>For a time-domain calculation, if the simulated response torque does not include both the engine mean torque and the propeller mean torque, obtain the response torque using Q_peak = Q_emax + Q_rtd (6.32), where Q_rtd is the maximum simulated torque from the time-domain analysis.</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
