    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for maximumContinuousRatingPower derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <nltl:sourceReference>TRF-006 | TRAFICOM p.5 | 1.6; TRF-017 | TRAFICOM p.7 | 3.1; TRF-018 | TRAFICOM p.8 | 3.2; TRF-020 | TRAFICOM p.8-9 | 3.2.2; TRF-023 | TRAFICOM p.10 | 3.2.3; TRF-037 | TRAFICOM p.14 | 4.2.2; TRF-039 | TRAFICOM p.15 | 4.2.2; TRF-130 | TRAFICOM p.62 | 7.2; TRF-132 | TRAFICOM p.64 | 8</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>The Board of Navigation Rules for Assigning Ships Separate Ice-Due Classes, 1985, (2.9.1985 No. 2575/85/307), as amended, apply to ships the keels of which have been laid or which have been at a similar stage of construction on or after 1 November 1986 but before 1 September 2003. On the owner's request, the requirements of the 2008 Ice Class Regulations may...</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
