    <nltl:namingRule>N3 - remove unit from the identifier and retain it in unit/quantity metadata</nltl:namingRule>
    <nltl:unitDecisionStatus>Verified recommended QUDT unit from Stage 1 or a documented Stage 2 source-unit refinement</nltl:unitDecisionStatus>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for dailyLowTemperature derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <nltl:sourceReference>IMO-011 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.13 | 1.2.9</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>Mean Daily Low Temperature (MDLT) means the mean value of the daily low temperature for each day of the year over a minimum 10 year period. A data set acceptable to the Administration may be used if 10 years of data is not available.</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
