    <nltl:unitDecisionStatus>Recommended canonical QUDT unit selected by Stage 2 engineering normalization: Canonical benchmark power unit</nltl:unitDecisionStatus>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for mainPower derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <nltl:sourceReference>IMO-086 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.27 | 9.3.2.2.1; IMO26-012 | IMO_AMEND_2026 p.4 | 9-1.3.2.2.1</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>Ships shall have two non-magnetic means to determine and display their heading. Both means shall be independent and shall be connected to the ship's main and emergency source of power.</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
    <skos:altLabel>main_power</skos:altLabel>
    <nltl:sourceAlias>main_power</nltl:sourceAlias>
    <nltl:sourceRequirementId>IMO-086</nltl:sourceRequirementId>
    <nltl:sourceRequirementId>IMO26-012</nltl:sourceRequirementId>
    <nltl:unitSymbol>kW</nltl:unitSymbol>
    <nltl:recommendedUnit rdf:resource="http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloW"/>
    <nltl:quantityKindLabel>Power</nltl:quantityKindLabel>
  </rdf:Description>
