    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Maximum ice torque</skos:prefLabel>
    <nltl:draftConceptId>VOC-0466</nltl:draftConceptId>
    <nltl:stage1LocalName>maximumIceTorque</nltl:stage1LocalName>
    <nltl:module rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#moduleMachinery"/>
    <nltl:roleDecisionBasis>Quantity metadata requires the canonical QUDT QuantityValue node pattern</nltl:roleDecisionBasis>
    <nltl:namingBasis>Unit-stripped normalized regulatory variable</nltl:namingBasis>
    <nltl:namingRule>N3 - remove unit from the identifier and retain it in unit/quantity metadata</nltl:namingRule>
    <nltl:unitDecisionStatus>Verified recommended QUDT unit from Stage 1 or a documented Stage 2 source-unit refinement</nltl:unitDecisionStatus>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for maximumIceTorque derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <nltl:sourceReference>TRF-069 | TRAFICOM p.26 | 6.1; TRF-092 | TRAFICOM p.40 | 6.5.3.4; TRF-095 | TRAFICOM p.40 | 6.5.3.4; TRF-098 | TRAFICOM p.44 | 6.5.3.4</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>These regulations apply to propulsion machinery covering open- and ducted-type propellers with a controllable pitch or fixed pitch design for ice classes IA Super, IA, IB and IC. The given propeller loads are the expected ice loads for the entire ship's service life under normal operational conditions, including loads resulting from the changing rotational d...</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
