    <nltl:unitDecisionStatus>Verified recommended QUDT unit from Stage 1 or a documented Stage 2 source-unit refinement</nltl:unitDecisionStatus>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for tankOuterShellSeparation derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <nltl:sourceReference>IMO-111 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.41 | 1.2.4</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>For category A and B ships constructed on or after 1 January 2017 all oil residue (sludge) tanks and oily bilge water holding tanks shall be separated from the outer shell by a distance of not less than 0.76 m. This provision does not apply to small tanks with a maximum individual capacity not greater than 30 m^3.</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
