    <nltl:stage1LocalName>engineFiringPulse</nltl:stage1LocalName>
    <nltl:module rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#moduleMachinery"/>
    <nltl:roleDecisionBasis>Conservative textual scalar fallback</nltl:roleDecisionBasis>
    <nltl:namingBasis>Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term</nltl:namingBasis>
    <nltl:namingRule>N5 - component or subject first, followed by characteristic and qualifier/state; no unsupported external mapping</nltl:namingRule>
    <nltl:unitDecisionStatus>Not a quantity property</nltl:unitDecisionStatus>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for engineFiringPulse derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <nltl:sourceReference>TRF-093 | TRAFICOM p.40 | 6.5.3.4</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>Diesel engine plants without an elastic coupling shall be calculated at the least favourable phase angle for ice versus engine excitation, when calculated in the time domain. The engine firing pulses shall be included in the calculations and their standard steady state harmonics can be used.</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
    <skos:altLabel>engineFiringPulse</skos:altLabel>
    <nltl:sourceAlias>engineFiringPulse</nltl:sourceAlias>
    <nltl:sourceRequirementId>TRF-093</nltl:sourceRequirementId>
