    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for actualFrameShearArea derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.</skos:definition>
    <nltl:sourceReference>TRF-048 | TRAFICOM p.20 | 4.4.3</nltl:sourceReference>
    <nltl:evidenceExcerpt>The section modulus of a longitudinal frame shall be calculated using Z = f_4*p*h*l^2/(4*m*sigma_y)*10^6 [cm^3] (4.9). The effective shear area shall be A = sqrt(3)*f_4*f_5*p*h*l/(2*sigma_y)*10^4 [cm^2] (4.10). The bracket shear area shall not be included in the actual frame shear area. Use f_4 = 1 - 0.2*h/s, f_5 = 2.16, p from 4.2.2, h from 4.2.1, s as fram...</nltl:evidenceExcerpt>
    <skos:altLabel>actual_frame_shear_area</skos:altLabel>
    <nltl:sourceAlias>actual_frame_shear_area</nltl:sourceAlias>
    <nltl:sourceRequirementId>TRF-048</nltl:sourceRequirementId>
    <nltl:unitSymbol>cm^2</nltl:unitSymbol>
